Title: Add a reranker to retrieval (Albert)
Created: 2026-11-01
Author: MinhHaDuong

--- log ---
2026-11-01T13:01Z MinhHaDuong created

--- body ---
Blocked-by: 0009

## Context
Author request, 2026-11-01. Retrieval today returns the vector search's top
chunks as they come (R2R, OpenAI embeddings); a reranker re-scores those
candidates against the question before generation, which usually lifts
answer quality and citation precision for a small latency cost. The author
wants it served by Albert, in line with ticket 0009 (Albert for embeddings,
retrieval and generation). To verify, not assumed: that Albert exposes a
rerank endpoint and which model, and whether it can run in the self-hosted
option of 0009.

Blocked by 0009 because where the reranker plugs in depends on the chosen
architecture (Albert end to end, Albert behind R2R, or self-hosted).

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Reranker wired into retrieval in the architecture chosen by 0009: retrieve N candidates, rerank, pass the top k to generation (N, k recorded)
- [ ] Measured on the 0009 fixed question set: citation precision and answer quality with and without the reranker, and the added latency
- [ ] Kept only if it improves quality at an acceptable latency; the decision and numbers recorded in this ticket
